jitAssignHolderT -- F-151, SEQ 575 (Tony, 2026-11-09): the trap outside EXPRESSIOn. An ordinary action, compiled by jitter;, whose
holder oaH is written by := inside an if-arm, then `oaT = oaH;`. Interpreted, the holder's group crosses and oaT reads 7. Compiled
today the = takes its scalar path and stores the holder's pointer bits as a count: 52032688 on the run that measured it, an
address, so it moves run to run (H3) and pop.sh pins it by class -- any value of 65536 or more reads "addr".

Not run alone: pop.sh appends, per arm, oaT = "pre", two calls, a print after, a sentinel; the compiled arm puts jitter; first.
